    // A is row-major [M, K], B is [K, 1], C is [M, 1]
    // cuBLASLt is column-major, so we describe:
    //   A_col = A^T => [K, M] col-major with ld=M  (but A is row-major [M,K] => treat as col-major [K,M] with ld=K)
    //   We want: C = A * B
    //   In col-major: C_col[M,1] = op(A_col) * B_col[K,1]
    //   A_col is [K,M] col-major (ld=K), op=TRANSPOSE => op(A_col) is [M,K]
    //   So: C_col[M,1] = A_col^T[M,K] * B_col[K,1]  -- correct!

